# Declared test toolchain — what CI's `tests` matrix installs.
#
# EDIT THIS FILE, then run `python3 scripts/lock_toolchain.py` to regenerate the
# hash-pinned `test-tools.txt` beside it.
#
# Resolved UNIVERSALLY from the >=3.9 floor, so one file covers the whole
# 3 OS x 3 Python matrix. uv emits environment markers per interpreter, which
# means 3.12/3.14 still get current pytest while 3.9 gets the last release that
# supported it — locking does not drag modern Pythons back to the floor's
# versions. Left unpinned here on purpose: the resolver picks the newest release
# valid for each interpreter, and `lock_toolchain.py` is when that choice gets
# made and reviewed.
pytest
pytest-cov
coverage
hypothesis
